Description:
    Declares a search index in config/search.rb and adds has_search to the model.

    Pass the model name and a list of field:type pairs. Types are
    <%= ActiveSearch::Index::Field::VALID_TYPES.join(", ") %>.

    A field with no type is text, because searching is the common intent and a
    string field is not searched. That is deliberately not the string default
    rails generate model uses.

    A third segment carries modifiers, the slot rails generate model uses for
    index. The modifier is multiple.

    The fields you name are the fields the index holds. Nothing is read from the
    table, because choosing what is searchable and what is filterable is the
    declaration rather than boilerplate.

Example:
    bin/rails generate active_search:index Article title body:text status:string

    Appends to config/search.rb:
        ActiveSearch.define_index(:articles) do
          text :title
          text :body
          string :status
        end

    And adds to app/models/article.rb:
        has_search

    bin/rails generate active_search:index Article commenters:string:multiple
